From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [DO NOT APPLY] security: allow AppArmor as a secondary LSM

Android vendor policy requires SELinux to remain the primary exclusive LSM,
while Ubuntu Touch click-app confinement requires AppArmor to initialize too.
The default flags make both LSMs exclusive, so SELinux-first disables AppArmor.
Make AppArmor a non-major secondary LSM; keep the device config's SELinux-first
ordering and default unchanged.

This device-specific stacking change is experimental and must be runtime-tested
before deployment.
---
 security/apparmor/lsm.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/security/apparmor/lsm.c b/security/apparmor/lsm.c
--- a/security/apparmor/lsm.c
+++ b/security/apparmor/lsm.c
@@ -1780,6 +1780,6 @@ DEFINE_LSM(apparmor) = {
 	.name = "apparmor",
-	.flags = LSM_FLAG_LEGACY_MAJOR | LSM_FLAG_EXCLUSIVE,
+	.flags = 0,
 	.enabled = &apparmor_enabled,
 	.blobs = &apparmor_blob_sizes,
 	.init = apparmor_init,
 };
